# expect.stdout: 42\n
# expect.exit: 0
# expect.xfail: feature_coverage.py runs through bootstrap_general.sscript which still treats `send`/`receive` as a no-op and a zero bind. Direct semsc.py compilation works correctly (`python compiler/semsc.py THIS_FILE --emit-exe /tmp/x.exe && /tmp/x.exe` prints `42\n` because the single-thread channel slot carries the value from send to receive). Closing means teaching bootstrap_general to alloca one i64 slot per channel and route send/receive through store/load.
project ChannelSendReceive
target console
runtime AgentRuntime 0.1
entry console main
error MainError
errorCase MainError Placeholder CSignedInt32
operation main
input operation main console Console
output operation main Result ExitCode MainError
effect main write console.stdout
memory main heap no
async main no
purpose operation main "Single-thread channel: send writes into the channel slot; receive reads it back."
invariant operation main "Output is the value that was sent (42), not the zero default."
label startMain
storage module immutable valueToSend I64 42
send messageBus valueToSend
receive deliveredValue I64 messageBus
call printDeliveredCall console.writeIntegerLine
argument printDeliveredCall console Console console
argument printDeliveredCall value I64 deliveredValue
run printDeliveredCall
ignore void source printDeliveredCall
storage module immutable successfulExitCode ExitCode 0
return ok successfulExitCode
